<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

`AutomergeDocStore` stands as the one `LarTiddlerStore` over an Automerge document: the shore where a record crosses into the CRDT's medium.

!! A field value rests as an immutable scalar

Every string of a record rests in the document as an Automerge immutable scalar: one operation per field. A plain string handed to Automerge rests as a Text object, one operation per character, and every peer that receives the document pays that cost again. A tiddler stands as an invariant and every write replaces a field whole, so nothing in the house edits a value at character grain.

Two doors hold the crossing. `stored-record.ts` wraps on the way in (`storedRecord`, `storedLarRecord`). `stored-value.ts` unwraps on the way out (`plainRecord`, `plainField`, `plainEntries`, `tiddlerText`) and imports no CRDT engine, so the wiki's packed modules read through it. `LarDoc.tiddlers` holds the type `StoredLarRecord`, which exposes no field: a reader that skips the read door does not compile, and `stored-value-census.test.ts` scans every source file for a cast that would talk past the type. The store hands every reader past the shore a frozen plain record, which crosses a worker port whole; a raw record does not.

!! Field grain

A write merges a record field by field at its base. A field whose value did not move takes no assignment, and Automerge writes no operation for a scalar set to an equal value. Two writers that set one field to different values leave a multi-value conflict that `parallel-drafts.ts` surfaces as attributed drafts; two writers that set different fields both land.

!! A removal no reader can keep refuses by name

''The store decides nothing and authors nothing'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings`>>). A based removal that drops fields a concurrent writer set leaves the concurrent values live in the merged record, and the hand's own record, without those fields, surfaces to each parallel-drafts reader, which keeps it beside the live record until a person settles the two. Where no parallel-drafts reader stands to keep the concurrent words, or every reader failed, the based removal refuses by name and nothing lands: the store writes no parallel draft of its own, since that draft would rest in a bag whose tier and steward the store never weighed. A reader's failure reads as no reader. The hand keeps its words in its own editor, reads the concurrent value and answers again against it, as a write over a stale base answers `conflict`.

''The refusal carries a durable conflict handle'': the document, the removal's request id, and the identities of the conflicting change and of the heads it stands against, and never the hand's text. A hand whose editor went offline finds the same conflict on its return under that handle.

''Owed.'' The store lands a based removal first and surfaces it after: with no reader it drops the surfacing with no word, and a reader that throws earns one console line while the write stands (`_surfaceRemoval`). The refusal before any change lands, and the handle's durable home, ride the roadmap's loop `G34`.

!! One change per family

`writeFamily` lands its puts and tombstones in one Automerge change, so a peer receives a root, its children and its orphans' tombstones together. LOAD hands the store a slice of whole carriers per call, so a LOAD slice lands as one change.

<<~/ahu>>

